WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.233
^Hey there,

00:00:01.233 --> 00:00:02.066
^I'm Claire

00:00:02.066 --> 00:00:02.899
^and I'm a tasty producer

00:00:02.899 --> 00:00:03.732
^and today I'm going to show you

00:00:03.732 --> 00:00:04.780
some of my favorite recipes

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:06.508
to make for the kids in my life.

00:00:06.508 --> 00:00:08.720
(energetic music)

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:09.553
Personally,

00:00:09.553 --> 00:00:10.800
I don't actually have kids,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.860
but my mom and I are the caregivers for

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:13.900
my six year old niece

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.190
and my three year old nephew.

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:16.023
Basically,

00:00:16.023 --> 00:00:16.970
I get to be this really cool

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:18.710
Auntie-Mom hybrid superhero

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:19.710
and it's hard,

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:20.710
but it's also really,

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:21.543
really rewarding.

00:00:21.543 --> 00:00:23.440
When they suddenly came into my care

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.310
I had to quickly learn how to cook for kids

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:26.830
and let me tell you,

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.220
it was no easy feat.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.280
I was lucky enough to be able to channel it into my work

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.350
by making Tasty videos

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.750
and Tasty Junior videos.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:33.890
My co-worker Hannah,

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.240
she has this six year old son,

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.110
his name is Jackson

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:37.000
and he's my best friend

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.350
and he's usually my sous chef

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:39.850
in all Tasty Junior videos.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.800
We have been cooking together since he was four

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.360
and I've gotten to see him blossom

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.620
into such a kind-hearted

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:46.530
and goofy boy.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:48.300
We have a blast together in the kitchen

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.870
and he brings so much joy to the office

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:50.870
whenever he comes in.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:52.070
So as all parents know,

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.900
you don't always have time to cook everything

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.300
in the morning during the week

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.709
and it was my nephew's birthday.

00:00:56.709 --> 00:00:58.601
I wanted to make something super innovative

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:00.870
and special for his birthday breakfast.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.330
And he loves cinnamon rolls

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:03.990
and who doesn't love birthday cake?

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.580
So I made a cinnamon roll out of birthday cake

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:07.780
and they were such a hit at home

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.434
that I had to make them into a Tasty Junior video.

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:10.267
Now,

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:11.810
I know what you all are thinking:

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:14.030
who gives their kid so much sugar for breakfast?

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:16.400
But just to see the joy of his face

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.810
when he woke up to a cinnamon roll birthday cake,

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:21.430
he was ecstatic

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:23.650
and it made the experience of making it

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:24.600
just that much better.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:25.433
So,

00:01:25.433 --> 00:01:27.855
in order to fuse cinnamon rolls

00:01:27.855 --> 00:01:29.430
and birthday cake together,

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:32.081
I had to figure out a way to get that cake flavor

00:01:32.081 --> 00:01:34.160
without adding extra sugar.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.468
I ended up just using a box of pre-made cake mix

00:01:37.468 --> 00:01:40.580
and adding flour to the cake mixture

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:42.340
to make it more of a dough consistency

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.290
rather than a cake batter consistency

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:45.620
and it worked like a charm.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:46.560
They're fluffy,

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:47.393
they're sweet,

00:01:47.393 --> 00:01:48.226
they're cake-y.

00:01:48.226 --> 00:01:50.660
They're everything you would want in a birthday cake

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:51.893
cinnamon roll hybrid.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.140
Having to all of a sudden pack lunches for two kids

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:57.902
was super intimidating at first.

00:01:57.902 --> 00:01:59.010
When I was a kid,

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.500
I remember getting made fun of

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.230
for having certain things in my lunch

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:03.660
and I really didn't want that for them,

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:06.210
but I still wanted them to have nutritious lunches,

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.700
which I know can be time consuming.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:09.430
My time is already so limited in the mornings,

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:10.990
and I needed a quick solution,

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:13.440
so I thought of how adults meal-prep for their week

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:14.273
all the time

00:02:14.273 --> 00:02:15.106
and so,

00:02:15.106 --> 00:02:16.160
I just adapted it for the kids.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.980
It teaches kids the responsibility

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:18.962
of packing their own lunch.

00:02:18.962 --> 00:02:21.590
My niece loved that responsibility

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.650
and she was so proud to walk up to her friends

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:25.810
and show them that she had made it for herself

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.900
and I could see the confidence growing inside of her

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.290
and it was great for me too

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.450
because doing just a little bit of preparation

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:33.890
can save you ten minutes of time in the morning.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:36.500
That extra ten minutes allowed me to

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.000
be able to brush my hair

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:39.680
or have a cup of coffee

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:42.743
or spend those extra few minutes with the kids.

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:44.300
And it also sometimes will give me

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.610
that extra ten minutes of sleep

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:47.100
which is so valuable.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.770
This is not the only thing that you can make

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.100
for your kids' lunches.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.330
Have it fit your needs.

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:54.770
It's all going to be catered to your family

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:55.800
and what your family likes,

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.850
but it's just designed to save you some time

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:00.500
and as much as it saves time for me,

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:03.400
it also teaches my niece some responsibility

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:06.110
to pack her own lunch is such a big deal

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:09.020
because she feels like she is serving a role.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:11.320
It gives her an opportunity to participate

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:12.700
in our morning routine

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.240
and she feels like she's a part of it

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.360
and that's really special for our family.

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:17.790
We want to include them

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:20.740
and raise them to be independent human beings

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:24.280
and this is just one of the ways in which she is learning

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:25.873
to be an independent person.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.742
Everybody has their go-to favorites

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:31.449
when they're cooking for their kids.

00:03:31.449 --> 00:03:32.810
In my house,

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.420
tacos hands-down are the winner,

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:36.630
but they're always such a mess

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:38.100
especially with a toddler.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:38.933
So,

00:03:38.933 --> 00:03:40.660
I was trying to figure out a way to work around it

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:42.630
and then the taco breadsticks were born.

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:43.980
Kids love tacos.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:44.960
Kids love breadsticks,

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:46.330
so why not combine them?

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.050
I know it's not traditional in any way,

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:48.883
shape,

00:03:48.883 --> 00:03:49.716
or form,

00:03:49.716 --> 00:03:51.140
but I really enjoy being able to

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:52.552
use inspiration from other classic dishes

00:03:52.552 --> 00:03:56.003
around the world to make them fit my family's needs.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:57.660
My nephew can hold it in his hand

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:59.564
and not make a mess all over the table

00:03:59.564 --> 00:04:01.033
or himself.

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:02.990
Getting a kid to try a new thing

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:04.380
can be really difficult

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.930
so if you play with their personal flavors

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:08.270
that you know that they like,

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:10.400
it will be much easier for them to eat it

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.010
if they know it's taco-flavored

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:13.030
or pizza-flavored

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.910
or something familiar to them,

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:15.830
but in a new form.

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:16.663
At my house,

00:04:16.663 --> 00:04:18.870
I serve them to my niece and nephew as an appetizer

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:19.703
or a snack

00:04:19.703 --> 00:04:20.890
or even a side at dinner.

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:23.030
They're just a special treat the kids love

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:24.040
and it blows their minds

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:25.923
just about every time they eat them.

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:27.773
Dinner is probably the number one,

00:04:27.773 --> 00:04:30.130
most frustrating thing for parents

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:31.220
when cooking for kids.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:32.530
It can take a lot of time

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:33.363
and effort

00:04:33.363 --> 00:04:34.830
and by the time you're done cooking,

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:36.750
they're probably just going to turn their nose up at it

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:37.930
and say it's not what they wanted.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:39.330
There was this one time I went to dinner with

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:40.163
my boyfriend

00:04:40.163 --> 00:04:41.636
and his family at this really nice,

00:04:41.636 --> 00:04:42.472
expensive,

00:04:42.472 --> 00:04:44.580
Japanese teppanyaki restaurant.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.940
There was this child across the table from us

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:50.530
whose parents had ordered him this really nice steak dinner

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.050
that was cooked right in front of him

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:53.520
and it was really exciting for him

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.900
but all he would eat was his fried rice.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.897
That's like 30 dollars worth of dinner

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:00.540
and all he ate was fried rice

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:01.430
and I was like dude,

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:02.766
you have such a great dinner in front of you,

00:05:02.766 --> 00:05:04.450
why are you only eating fried rice?

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:05.550
And then it dawned on me.

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:07.083
Kids love fried rice, duh.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:10.110
So that experience inspired me to create fried rice

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.060
and to play with the flavors of fried rice

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:12.893
because yes,

00:05:12.893 --> 00:05:14.230
it's not traditional again,

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.620
but it is an opportunity for me to show

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.110
my creativity through the food that I make for the kids.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:19.943
I don't know about you,

00:05:19.943 --> 00:05:21.710
but I never met a kid who doesn't like fried rice.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:23.380
So if you can play with the flavors

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:25.649
and customize it to your child's preference,

00:05:25.649 --> 00:05:28.313
you've got a solid hit for dinner that night.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:29.387
As much as we would like to be,

00:05:29.387 --> 00:05:31.380
we can't always be model parents

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:33.280
and our kids can't always be model children.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:34.113
Luckily,

00:05:34.113 --> 00:05:35.024
my niece and nephew are perfect

00:05:35.024 --> 00:05:37.310
and they usually eat their vegetables,

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.210
but sometimes I do have to get creative.

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:40.043
With this dish,

00:05:40.043 --> 00:05:42.300
I really wanted to take the classic,

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.150
childhood favorite of a cheeseburger

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:47.370
and bring it to life with a little bit of healthiness to it.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:48.430
I added some broccoli

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:49.263
and carrots.

00:05:49.263 --> 00:05:50.096
Honestly,

00:05:50.096 --> 00:05:51.270
I don't even think the kids noticed

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:52.370
that there was anything in there.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:53.830
They're not little investigators

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.220
like I know some kids can be,

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:56.600
but I know these kids

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:59.440
and I know that if there was a plate with broccoli

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:00.273
and carrots

00:06:00.273 --> 00:06:01.440
and a cheeseburger on it,

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:02.273
those broccoli

00:06:02.273 --> 00:06:03.730
and carrots probably will get ignored.

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:04.780
Believe it or not,

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:05.900
I do read the comments.

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:08.570
I've noticed a lot of parents shaming other parents

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:12.140
for having to hide their vegetables in their kids' food

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:14.480
and if that's what works for their family,

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:15.313
great.

00:06:15.313 --> 00:06:16.146
If it doesn't work for yours,

00:06:16.146 --> 00:06:17.120
try something else.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:18.695
And if you have a perfect child who eats every vegetable

00:06:18.695 --> 00:06:19.810
that crosses their path,

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.360
you my friend,

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:22.193
are a lucky parent.

00:06:22.193 --> 00:06:23.210
If you're still finding it hard

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:25.300
to get the kids to eat something that has green in it,

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:27.130
try involving them in the cooking process.

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:28.830
They're more likely to eat what they made

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:30.430
because they have a sense of pride in it

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:33.180
and you get a good bonding experience cooking together.

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:36.570
I am a mean baker,

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:38.220
but I am not the best cake decorator

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:40.360
so I was looking for something pretty full-proof

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:42.520
that even I could make for my niece's birthday.

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:43.726
When we were planning her fifth birthday party,

00:06:43.726 --> 00:06:46.070
I'd ask her what theme she wanted

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:47.620
and all she would say was unicorn,

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:48.453
that was it.

00:06:48.453 --> 00:06:49.286
It was going to be unicorns

00:06:49.286 --> 00:06:50.610
and she would accept nothing else.

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:53.120
The kids had recently started living with me

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:54.580
and she didn't know that many kids

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.400
and she was new to the area

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:58.090
and I really wanted to give her

00:06:58.935 --> 00:06:59.930
the most amazing birthday possible.

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:00.860
She's such a great kid

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:02.100
and she's been through so much,

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.790
that she really does deserve the best.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.590
I went from being a free-spirit,

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:07.450
easy-going 24-year-old woman

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:09.500
living with my best friend in Los Angeles

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:10.650
to a parent.

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:11.780
Basically overnight

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:12.990
and I'm not going to lie,

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.010
it was terrifying

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:15.620
and it still is terrifying

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:17.710
because I have these two amazing little people

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:20.280
who rely on me for everything in their lives.

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:22.180
We've had a lot of opportunities

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:23.470
to learn from one another

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:26.015
and they have made just as much of an impact on my life

00:07:26.015 --> 00:07:28.186
as I feel like I have made on theirs.

00:07:28.186 --> 00:07:30.473
I don't know if I personally will ever have kids,

00:07:30.473 --> 00:07:31.540
but,

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:34.410
I will say that I am more than happy to give all my love

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:36.280
to these two kids for the rest of our days.

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:37.200
I'm not gonna lie

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.000
and say any of this has been easy,

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.370
it's been the most difficult time in my life so far,

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:44.521
but I wouldn't trade a second of it for the world.

00:07:44.521 --> 00:07:47.420
Even though I'm not their biological parent,

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:50.710
I still have to face the day to day activities

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:52.280
that parents do with their kids.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:53.480
I made this amazing cake

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:55.400
and I brought it out to all the kids at the party

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:56.880
and they were all so excited,

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:59.280
the cake got devoured in about ten minutes.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:00.670
On the way home from her party,

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:02.870
she had said thank you so many times,

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:03.703
but she says auntie,

00:08:03.703 --> 00:08:05.930
you know I loved my unicorn cake,

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:07.070
but I just want you to know

00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:09.303
that it did kind of look like cow too.

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:11.420
And when the video got posted on the internet,

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:13.460
the commenters also thought it looked like a cow,

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:15.360
which it was not as cute coming from them,

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:16.840
but it was adorable coming from her.

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:17.673
So yes,

00:08:17.673 --> 00:08:18.506
It does look like a cow,

00:08:18.506 --> 00:08:19.339
but it's a unicorn cow

00:08:19.339 --> 00:08:20.172
and it's unique.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:23.043
These two little kids are the most creative

00:08:23.043 --> 00:08:24.360
and quirky

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.080
and funny people I've ever met.

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:27.520
If I can foster that

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:29.840
and channel it into being inventive

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:30.673
and cooking

00:08:30.673 --> 00:08:31.790
and being creative with me,

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:33.930
that's the best activity we could ever do together.

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:34.763
Food is my love language

00:08:34.763 --> 00:08:36.490
and it's how I show the people in my life

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:37.544
that I care about them.

00:08:37.544 --> 00:08:41.370
Cooking for these kids has been such a journey

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.640
of trial and error

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:44.220
and it's made me a better cook

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:45.550
and a better aunt because of it

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:48.730
and I just have adored every second of this journey.

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:49.563
That's not true,

00:08:49.563 --> 00:08:50.396
I've complained a lot,

00:08:50.396 --> 00:08:51.229
but it's fine.

00:08:51.269 --> 00:08:52.269
(offscreen) Oh, yes.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:54.550
(laughter)

00:08:54.819 --> 00:08:57.986
(gentle guitar music)

